  "name": "OntoBoard",
  "description": "A Protégé Desktop plugin that brings the ODK and ROBOT ontology-engineering workflow into the editor: scaffold an Ontology Development Kit project, build it, run ROBOT's report, explain what the reasoner concluded, refresh imports, edit ROBOT template spreadsheets and cut a release — all against the ontology already open in Protégé. ROBOT (robot-core 1.9.8) is embedded as a library and its operations run in-process, so the common ones need no terminal, no make and no container. The plugin ships as a single OSGi bundle dropped into Protégé's plugins folder.",
